[
    {
        "content": "<p>Related to the previous discussion about <code>ULift</code>, we have <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=LinearMap.pi#doc\">docs#LinearMap.pi</a>, <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=ContinuousMap.pi#doc\">docs#ContinuousMap.pi</a> on the one hand, but <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Pi.monoidHom#doc\">docs#Pi.monoidHom</a> and <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Pi.algHom#doc\">docs#Pi.algHom</a>. Which one do we prefer?</p>",
        "id": 598538630,
        "sender_full_name": "Anatole Dedecker",
        "timestamp": 1780054455
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>/poll Which spelling ?<br>\nPi.fooHom<br>\nFooHom.pi</p>",
        "id": 598538975,
        "sender_full_name": "Anatole Dedecker",
        "timestamp": 1780054581
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Here I have a quite strong preference for <code>FooHom.pi</code>, motivated by the analogy with <code>FooHom.prod</code> (and we can't change <code>FooHom.prod</code> since we like dot notation)</p>",
        "id": 598539203,
        "sender_full_name": "Anatole Dedecker",
        "timestamp": 1780054660
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>FWIW after <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/pull/13244\">lean4#13244</a> we could have dot notation by using <code>Function.fooHom</code>, but I don't think it's worth it</p>",
        "id": 598540192,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1780055023
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>How would that look in practice ?</p>",
        "id": 598540436,
        "sender_full_name": "Anatole Dedecker",
        "timestamp": 1780055107
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=AlgHom.prod#doc\">docs#AlgHom.prod</a> and <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=MonoidHom.prod#doc\">docs#MonoidHom.prod</a> are already a thing , so <code>Pi.algHom</code> feels just wrong to me</p>",
        "id": 598540671,
        "sender_full_name": "Moritz Doll",
        "timestamp": 1780055201
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"268315\">Anatole Dedecker</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/Pi.2EfooHom.20or.20FooHom.2Epi/near/598540436\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>How would that look in practice ?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>After that PR is merged, if we rename <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Pi.monoidHom#doc\">docs#Pi.monoidHom</a> to <code>Function.monoidHom</code> then with <code>(g : (i : I) → γ →* f i)</code> the homomorphism would be <code>g.monoidHom</code>.<br>\nCurrently the issue is that such dot-notation would set <code>(f := g)</code> instead of <code>(g := g)</code>, since <code>f</code> is the first function parameter.</p>",
        "id": 598543785,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1780056225
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>This one seems a bit evil to me</p>",
        "id": 598546189,
        "sender_full_name": "Anatole Dedecker",
        "timestamp": 1780057052
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Indeed</p>",
        "id": 598550785,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1780058397
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/40024\">#40024</a> starts this process. I'm also happy to wait if you think larger consensus is necessary</p>",
        "id": 598601212,
        "sender_full_name": "Anatole Dedecker",
        "timestamp": 1780072584
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Is there a good place to document this decision (whatever it is)? I'd like us to get better at recording naming rules :-)</p>",
        "id": 598631632,
        "sender_full_name": "Michael Rothgang",
        "timestamp": 1780083202
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Even a meta-thread collecting past naming decisions would already help. (There a private reviewers' repository, for instance --- not a great place, but much better that not collected!)</p>",
        "id": 598631728,
        "sender_full_name": "Michael Rothgang",
        "timestamp": 1780083241
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Why not just put it in <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/contribute/naming.html\">#naming</a> ?</p>",
        "id": 598632764,
        "sender_full_name": "Jireh Loreaux",
        "timestamp": 1780083639
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Eventually, would it make sense to split <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/contribute/naming.html\">#naming</a> into \"generic\" and \"specific\" ? Where \"specific\" would just be a list/dictionnary of naming decisions ?</p>",
        "id": 598638390,
        "sender_full_name": "Anatole Dedecker",
        "timestamp": 1780086132
    }
]